<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salomon Gessner</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1730–<a href="/years/1788">1788</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Salomon Gessner was a Swiss poet, painter and engraver from Zürich. His prose Idylls of 1756, pastoral scenes of innocent shepherds, were translated into many languages and made him one of the most widely read German-language authors of his day. He also ran a publishing house and illustrated his own works.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/salomon-gessner.jpg" alt="Salomon Gessner" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anton Graff · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anton_Graff_Salomon_Gessner.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
